},
{
["key"] = "q:96899:complete:267008",
["envelope"] = "!SPOKEN1 quests\naddon=SpokenQuests/3.8.0\nbuild=1.60.1/70790\nlocale=enUS\npack=enUS\npackVersion=2.5.0\nquest=96899\nevent=complete\nnpc=267008 Leonid Barthalomew the Revered\nkind=creature\nmodel=959310\nsex=2\ncreature=Humanoid\ntitle=Bandarion Keep\ntext<<\nThis place is full of memories for me. This place was once held by the Argent Dawn. It was from here that we prepared for many battles and skirmishes against the Scourge during their most recent push into Tirisfal Glades.\n\nWhen we withdrew to the Plaguelands I feared it would fall into disrepair. My fear was well-founded, but I am glad that Danitha and her paladins have taken over stewardship of it now.\n\nShe even named the keep after... a mutual friend.\n>>\nsum=1025035763\n",
},
{
["key"] = "q:96896:accept:267008",
["envelope"] = "!SPOKEN1 quests\naddon=SpokenQuests/3.8.0\nbuild=1.60.1/70790\nlocale=enUS\npack=enUS\npackVersion=2.5.0\nquest=96896\nevent=accept\nnpc=267008 Leonid Barthalomew the Revered\nkind=creature\nmodel=959310\nsex=2\ncreature=Humanoid\ntitle=A Righteous Cause\ntext<<\nDanitha and I fought against the Scourge in the defense of the Undercity when Naxxramas attacked. We lost many good friends that day, including the hero after which this keep was named--Garek Bandarion.\n\nHe might just have been the first Forsaken to rediscover how to wield the Light as a paladin. I am encouraged to see his legacy and potential live on here with Danitha and her cohort.\n\nIf only the rest of the Forsaken felt the same way...\n>>\nsum=369399075\n",
},
{
["key"] = "q:96896:complete:267008",
